<title>USA: Bausch &amp; Lomb gains FDA approval for lens.</title>
<headline>Bausch &amp; Lomb gains FDA approval for lens.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bausch &amp; Lomb Inc said Friday it had received approval from the Food and Drug Administration to market its SofLens66 contact lenses for extended wear of up to seven days.</p>
<p>The company said the lenses may be prescribed for either daily wear or extended wear from one to seven days between removal for cleaning and disinfection or disposal of the lenses.</p>
<p>Bausch &amp; Lomb had launched the lenses nationally last June.</p>
<p>It said it would make available in early 1997 a product labeled for extended wear once the administration had received the printed package labeling.</p>
</text>
